--TEST--
a `Throwable`'s synthesized constructor is callable by name like any other member — `message:` on its own, and `options: {previous: …}` for the chain (`rule:core-api/shape-rules` R2, spec § 10)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:errors/constructing-and-subclassing
// The constructor is `constructor(string $message, {previous?: Throwable|null})`
// and nothing about it is special-cased: the required parameter is `$message`.
try {
    throw new LogicError(message: "by name");
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}

// The bag is `options` here for the reason it is `options` at a `Core` member:
// being callable by that one name is a property of being a bag.
try {
    try {
        throw new RuntimeError(message: "cause");
    } catch (RuntimeError $inner) {
        throw new LogicError(message: "wrapper", options: {previous: $inner});
    }
} catch (LogicError $outer) {
    echo $outer->message, "\n";
    echo $outer->previous?->message ?? "none", "\n";
}

// And the bag stays optional by construction: naming the message alone leaves
// `previous` null rather than unfilled.
try {
    throw new LogicError(message: "alone");
} catch (LogicError $solo) {
    echo $solo->previous?->message ?? "none", "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
by name
wrapper
cause
none
